@startuml lockfree-try-set-final-race
' ============================================================================
' lockfree-try-set-final-race.puml — two threads insert the SAME term "hello".
' The finalization is decided by ONE atomic fetch_or on the shared final node's
' flags: exactly one caller flips IS_FINAL from 0→1 and returns true (inserted);
' every other caller observes it already set and returns false (already exists).
' The root-CAS + retry is folded into each thread's self-step to keep 3 lanes.
' Source: §Finalization Race Handling of lockfree-cas-artrie.md.
' Color key (house palette):
'   green  #2E7D32  the winner (fetch_or flips 0→1 → inserted)
'   red    #C62828  the loser (already final → returns false)
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #37474F
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam participantBorderColor #37474F
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
skinparam noteBorderColor #90A4AE

title try_set_final race — both insert "hello"; one atomic fetch_or picks the winner

participant "T1" as T1
participant "final node\nflags (atomic)" as F #C8E6C9
participant "T2" as T2

T1 -> T1 : build "hello"\nCAS root → new (wins)
T2 -> T2 : CAS fails → retry\nrebuild → CAS (wins)

== single arbiter: fetch_or(IS_FINAL) on the shared final node ==
T1 -> F : try_set_final()\n= fetch_or(IS_FINAL)
F -[#2E7D32]-> T1 : old bit = 0\n→ true (inserted)
T2 -> F : try_set_final()\n= fetch_or(IS_FINAL)
F -[#C62828]-> T2 : old bit = 1\n→ false (already exists)

note over T1, T2 #FFF9C4
  A proper-prefix insert returns the EXISTING
  shared node un-finalized, so fetch_or is the
  SINGLE arbiter — the fix that stopped a racing
  prefix term from being dropped at merge.
end note
@enduml
